			'---\nname: createPermission\ndescription: Creates a permission for a file or shared drive.\n---\n\n# Create Permission\n\nCreates a new permission for a file or shared drive using `POST /files/{fileId}/permissions`. This grants access to a user, group, domain, or anyone.\n\n## Role and Type Combinations\n\n| Type | Applicable Roles |\n|---|---|\n| `user` | owner, organizer, fileOrganizer, writer, commenter, reader |\n| `group` | organizer, fileOrganizer, writer, commenter, reader |\n| `domain` | organizer, fileOrganizer, writer, commenter, reader |\n| `anyone` | writer, commenter, reader |\n\n- **`emailAddress`** is required when type is `user` or `group`.\n- **`domain`** is required when type is `domain`.\n- **`transferOwnership`** must be `true` when setting role to `owner`.\n- **`allowFileDiscovery`** only applies to `domain` and `anyone` types.\n\n## Notification Emails\n\nWhen sharing with users or groups, a notification email is sent by default. Set `sendNotificationEmail` to `false` to suppress it. Use `emailMessage` to include a custom plain text message.\n\n## Shared Drive Support\n\nShared drive support is always enabled (`supportsAllDrives` is hardcoded to `true`). Shared drive roles like `organizer` and `fileOrganizer` are only valid for shared drive items.\n\n## Response\n\nReturns the created Permission resource.\n',
