			"---\nname: updateRevision\ndescription: Updates metadata for a file revision.\n---\n\n# Update Revision\n\nUpdates the metadata of a specific file revision using `PATCH /files/{fileId}/revisions/{revisionId}`.\n\n## Recommended Workflow\n\n1. Use `getRevision` to retrieve the current revision state.\n2. Modify the desired fields.\n3. Call this endpoint to apply changes.\n\n## Key Behavior\n\n- Only the fields provided in the request body are updated.\n- **`keepForever`**: Set to `true` to prevent automatic deletion of old revisions. By default, Google Drive may purge old revisions to free up storage.\n- **`published`**: Only applicable to Google Docs Editors files (Docs, Sheets, Slides). Makes the revision publicly accessible via the published link.\n- **`publishAuto`**: When `true`, future revisions are automatically published as well.\n- **`publishedOutsideDomain`**: Controls whether the published revision is visible to users outside the file owner's domain.\n\n## Response\n\nReturns the updated Revision resource.\n",
